# Testing Rules

- Name tests after behaviour, and cite the rule when one exists: `it('BR-14-03 expires a seat offer after 48 h', …)`.
- Arrange with factories (`test/factories/*`), never with raw JSON copied from fixtures; one assertion topic per test.
- No sleeps: use fake timers (`vi.useFakeTimers`) or await the condition.

## Server (Vitest)
- Unit tests mock repositories/engines, not Prisma internals.
- Integration tests use Supertest against `createApp()` with Testcontainers Postgres + Redis; each endpoint has happy path, authz denial (403/404 by scope) and validation (422) cases.
- Assert on `error.code`, not on message text.

## Frontend (Vitest + Testing Library + MSW)
- Render through `renderWithProviders` (store + router + i18n); query by role/label, not by class or test id unless unavoidable.
- MSW handlers live in `src/test/msw/handlers/<module>.ts` and return the API envelope shape.
- Playwright e2e only for the critical paths in doc 04; keep them data-independent via seeded personas.

## Mobile (jest-expo)
- Mock native modules (`expo-location`, `expo-camera`, `expo-secure-store`) in `jest.setup.ts`; never call real device APIs in tests.
- Offline-queue tests cover enqueue, replay order, and 409 handling.

## Coverage gates
- server ≥ 80 % (auth/engines ≥ 90 %), frontend ≥ 70 %, app ≥ 70 %; do not lower thresholds to pass CI.
